  "notes": [
    "THE ROLL OF FRIENDS (client/scenes/pages/friends_page.gd), built on YOUR LORDSHIP's own page (profile/page, the panel with everything inside the frame cleared) from the pieces the painting already has: its title and rule, its box, its friend row, its GIFT plate and its CLOSE. There is no painting of a friends page; there is a painting of friends, at the foot of profile.png, and this is that object given the whole page.",
    "A row is one lord: the ring with their face in it (the painted ring's window, 88 across), the green light only when they are here, their name in the steel box, what a gift would be worth to them in the gold one, and GIFT -- which is erased from the painted row, so a lord who has already had today's draught simply does not wear it.",
    "A lord who has asked to be a friend wears the same row with YES and NO in GIFT's place: the answer is where the gift would be, because it is the same question -- will you have this lord on your roll.",
    "Both lists live in one scroll: the asks first, because they are the thing waiting on you.",
    "The page stretches where the panel is the same all the way down (the list's own middle, and the gap above CLOSE): a taller phone shows more rows rather than the same page floating in the middle of its screen. The scroll across the first band grows with it."
  ],
